{"name":"Sour Tarts","hex":"#fee5c8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of acidity.","Made rancid by fermentation, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sensation of a sour taste.","A drink made with whiskey, lemon or lime juice and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour"},{"term":"tarts","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tart"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of tart"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tarts"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sourness","blocks":[{"text":"Sourness, also known as sour, is a basic taste sensation perceived through hydrogen ions from acidic compounds interacting with taste bud receptors, and it can also refer to an unpleasant or acidic quality in taste, disposition, or tone. It is a warning sign for potentially spoiled food, though it is balanced in some food products by sweetness, and it is associated with a low pH."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_with_white_background.jpg/330px-Lemon_with_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourness"},{"title":"Tart","blocks":[{"text":"A tart is a baked dish consisting of a filling over a pastry base with an open top not covered with pastry. The pastry is usually shortcrust pastry; the filling may be sweet or savoury, though modern tarts are usually fruit-based, sometimes with custard. Tartlet refers to a miniature tart; an example would be egg tarts. The categories of \"tart\", \"flan\", and \"pie\" overlap, with no sharp distinctions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Raspberry_tart.jpg/330px-Raspberry_tart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tart"}],"images":[{"srcset":"ht